#
# WHAT MOVED AND WHAT DID NOT
#   The ENCODE side moved and the DECODE side largely did not. `core-ffi-rust` encode is
#   0.10 to 0.27 above its published value on P1.1, P1.2, P2.2, P2.3 and P2.5 and inside the
#   published band on P1.3 and P2.4; every `core-ffi-rust` DECODE row except P1.3 and P2.1 is
#   within about 0.06 of its published band, and three are inside it. `armonik` -- prost's
#   own codec over the facade types, whose code this slice has not changed -- moved by up to
#   0.2 on M1 and by almost nothing on M2. No single arm's code explains that pattern, which
#   is the reason this log does not name a cause.
#
# ============================================================================
# THE THREE QUALITATIVE FINDINGS, RE-CONFIRMED
# ============================================================================
#   1. THE SIGN OF THE P1.3 INVERSION: CONFIRMED, and the magnitude is inside the published
#      band on encode. `core-ffi-rust` 1.190-1.210 encode and 1.623-1.858 decode against
#      `core-native` at 0.416-0.424 and 0.946-1.062. The absent path still turns a win in
#      both directions into a loss in both, and the group is still the explanation
#      (`stage3-inlining-term.log` audited the alternative away).
#   2. UTF-8 VALIDATION ON NON-ASCII: CONFIRMED, and LARGER than published. The scalar
#      validator reads 2.783 and 3.743 of prost on P1.2 latin1 and wide, 2.750 and 2.747 on
#      P2.2, against a published 2.0-2.6. The SIMD validator with the same contract recovers
#      it to 1.430-1.795 against a published 1.27-1.50.
#      **And the within-arm form of that finding reproduces almost exactly**: against its own
#      ASCII cost the scalar validator is 2.545 and 3.365 on P1.2, 2.169 and 2.679 on P2.2,
#      against a published "2.2 to 3.0 times its own ASCII cost". That is R4's new half
#      demonstrated rather than argued: the `/ prost` column moved and the delta taken
#      between two rows of the SAME ARM in the SAME PROCESS held.
#   3. DECODE CONVERGING TO PARITY AS AN ELEMENT GAINS CONTAINERS: CONFIRMED, same ordering.
#      `core-ffi-rust` decode 0.861 on P1.2 (6 blobs, 2 optional messages) and 0.978 on P2.2
#      (4 `Vec<String>`, a `BTreeMap`, a 27-field struct), with `core-native` at 0.875 and
#      0.911. The denser the element's container graph, the smaller the share of a decode any
#      codec owns.
#
# ============================================================================
# WHAT THIS DOES NOT ESTABLISH
# ============================================================================
#   - Why the published figures differ. Not checkable: the code is not in the repository at
#     that commit, and a different physical host cannot be ruled in or out from inside a
#     container.
#   - Anything about M3 to M7, which were not in this sweep.
#   - A distribution in any statistical sense. Three builds, six runs, min/median/max.
#   - That today's figures will reproduce in a month. The only claim is that they reproduce
#     across three builds and six runs in one session, which is what R4 now asks for.

