# =============================================================================
# APPENDIX A: the two artifact facts the verdict rests on
# =============================================================================
#
# A1. THE RELEASE BINARY IS BIT-IDENTICAL ACROSS REBUILDS OF UNCHANGED SOURCE, which is why
#     the layout perturbation exists at all:
#
#       $ cargo build --release -p harness --bin bench && sha256sum target/release/bench
#       90d08e36d17173be...
#       $ touch crates/harness/src/lib.rs
#       $ cargo build --release -p harness --bin bench && sha256sum target/release/bench
#       90d08e36d17173be...
#
# A2. THE COMMIT THAT PRODUCED THE PUBLISHED TABLE CANNOT BE BUILT. `cc7f68c6` is the stage 2
#     commit behind `stage2-four-arms-M1.log`:
#
#       $ git worktree add .../s2-wt cc7f68c6
#       $ cargo build --release -p harness --bin bench
#       error: can't find bin `bench` at path `crates/harness/src/bin/bench.rs`
#
#     Because the measurement binaries were untracked until `7fb30be5` -- the root
#     `.gitignore`'s `[Bb]in/`, defect D19. Confirmed by counting them in each tree:
#
#       cc7f68c6: 0     d03c5161: 0     7fb30be5: 7     160c37be: 9
#
#     And the dependency versions are identical at every one of those commits
#     (prost 0.14.4, bytes 1.12.1), so no bump is in play.
#
#     **This is D19 biting.** It was recorded as a hygiene defect -- "the logs were committed
#     and the code that produced them was not" -- and the cost of it is exactly this: a
#     published table that cannot be re-derived when it is questioned.

